{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Tips on IT Procurement: Protect Intellectual Property"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about Intellectual Property in IT procurement."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Create a report on fulfilment of terms of reference, cased on the participation of each agent in regards to the satisfaction of IT goods contracted and received, according to rules and protocols of the organization."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Writes simple texts on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, technological negotiation, and requirements on negotiation processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive voice in simple present and with modal verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>The <strong>passive voice </strong>is normally used when the importance is given to the object of the sentence and either we don&rsquo;t know who the agent of an action is or it is not important.</p> <p>In formal contexts both the <strong>simple present</strong> and <strong>modal verbs</strong> are used in this voice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <strong>passive voice</strong> is used in the <strong>simple present</strong> to talk about situations that occur on a regular basis. The verb to be in the present simple is used as the auxiliary followed by the main verb in its past participle form.</p> <p>When it is expected that something needs to be done by someone at any time, you use the passive form of the modal verb <strong>should</strong>.</p> <p>If it is ok to do something or it is possible you use the passive voice of the modal verb <strong>can</strong>. While, to express possibility you can use the passive voice of the modals <strong>might</strong> and <strong>may.</strong></p> <p>The passive voice of the modal verb <strong>must</strong> is used to express obligation.</p> <p>Examples:</p> <ul> <li><i>An special license <strong>should be acquired</strong> if you want to modify the sofware core features.</i></li> <li><i>The use of someone's IP <strong>can be legally performed</strong> under a special license.</i></li> <li><i>Anyhow you want to make use of the software, a license <strong>must be required</strong>.</i></li> </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When acquiring software, one of the main things customers have to be worried about is the risk of Intellectual property infringement."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Forethought should also be provided to the right to sublicense, including to other IT suppliers. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should be informed that their insurance will cover your from any damages that can caused by a claim made.   "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In general terms, IP mustn't be assigned away."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Intellectual Property Licenses "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Intellectual Property Licensing</strong> gives customers the right to use, but not possess, the IP.&nbsp;</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The two main kinds of Intellectual Property Licenses are <strong>Exclusive, Non-exclusive </strong>and <strong>Sole License</strong></p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Exclusive License\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"With this kind of license neither person nor company different from the licensee can capitalize on the relevant intellectual property rights. If the licensor is interested in conducting any venture covered in the intellectual property, the exclusive license needs to expressly state that it is exclusive subject to those exceptions. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Sole License \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This kind of license is also exclusive but the licensor reserves full rights to capitalize on the intellectual property itself. The licensor cannot grant any other sub-licenses.  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Non-exclusive License\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Confers the licensee the right to use the intellectual property, allowing the licensor and others to exploit the same intellectual property. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "assignment "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the transfer of a right to another party"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In order to be the owner of intellectual property in software or other supplier deliverables you need an express assignment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "forethought "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "consideration, deliberation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Forethought should also be provided to the right to sublicense, including to other IT suppliers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "insurance "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "agreement of reimbursement in case of loss"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As a customer you should obtain a warranty to prevent this and an indemnity from the supplier against similar claims, and you should be informed that their insurance will cover you from any damages that can be caused by a claim made.   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Intellectual Property Infringement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "violation of an intellectual property right  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When acquiring software, one of the main things customers have to be worried about is the risk of Intellectual property infringement.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "license "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to grant or give a permission for an activity "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If there is no agreement to prevent the opposite, suppliers can license the work you paid them to develop to your competitor. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "third party "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who is not directly involved in an agreement "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, having a license from a supplier doesn't always protect you from infringing a third party's intellectual property rights."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le03ob12aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about intellectual property protection when purchasing technological tools."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of tips and strategy about IP protection."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster presenting your ideas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your poster to your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about IP protection."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of tips for IP protection."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a poster with my tips."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my poster to my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand written information about intellectual property in IT procurement. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can use expressions related to intellectual property in IT procurement."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can write a simple text about protecting intellectual property for the company I work for."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think intellectual property is important when it comes to IT procurement and development? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What legal mechanisms do you know for the protection of intellectual property? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "