i": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le03ob12re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n7le03ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Intellectual property in IT Procurement</strong></p>\n<p>When acquiring software, one of the main things customers have to be worried about is the risk of Intellectual property infringement. The scope of a software license is the main thing to have in mind. Pay careful attention to the uses allowed under the license, including location, field, and number of users, since you, as the licensee, may need to buy additional licenses. Forethought should also be provided to the right to sublicense, including to other IT suppliers.</p>"}, {"time": "33000", "image": "enpe8n7le03ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p>Most of the times, it is a good idea to have a broad license with a fee consequence of increased use, instead of a narrow license that requires negotiation if use is increased. If you sign a purchase order and do not negotiate an express license then, how you use the software will be unclear.</p>\n<p>In order to be the owner of intellectual property in software or other supplier deliverables, you need an express assignment. Sometimes clients are surprised to know that they do not own a product they have developed and invested time and efforts on. If there is no agreement to prevent the opposite, suppliers can license the work you paid them to develop to your competitor.</p>"}, {"time": "72000", "image": "enpe8n7le03ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p>Some suppliers even try to make the customer assign intellectual property rights in the deliverables to the supplier. In general terms, IP mustn't be assigned away. You can also obtain an exclusive license that will give you exclusive rights to exploit the intellectual property rights.</p>\n<p>However, having a license from a supplier doesn't always protect you from infringing a third party's intellectual property rights. As a customer, you should obtain a warranty to prevent this and an indemnity from the supplier against similar claims, and you should be informed that their insurance will cover you from any damages that can be caused by a claim made.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le03ob12re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 5, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n7le03ob12re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}